    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:49b18e3fb3f9ec7b",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "50082839a8b1de5ec7b21d6053eb60d10f03bccd50e69a10ef8a28ab1df15b60",
      "text": "Breakfast. Transfer to the airport and flight to Caracas.\n\nMeet and depart for the historic Santa Teresa Estate, home to Venezuela’s finest rum. The estate was founded in 1796 by Martín Tovar Blanco and is located about an hour’s drive from Caracas, in a valley with unique climatic conditions ideal for growing sugar cane.\n\nIn 1802, the Tovar family was granted the title of Princes by the King of Spain in recognition of the exceptional quality of their rum.\n\nUpon arrival, we’ll tour the sugarcane plantations and the rum distillery, followed by a rum tasting in the Creadero de Solera cellars.\n\nOptional: cocktail-making master class and an opportunity to purchase premium Santa Teresa 1796 rum or the coffee-infused Araku rum.\n\nReturn to Caracas. Check-in at the hotel and rest.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "word_exact",
        "fileId": "1plVC8qsZFrF18IxEFHPNBR30SC37IQ_t",
        "documentSha256": "8b89afac8d3f74c0ce78fe5fb6992e5f749f67932c133c76fddb175809bbe29c",
